{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/config.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:58:58.925377Z","id":"6011cecd1752156802dacadc92021f4cdb331a0735a154c7d2498418156e9151","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-27-sizzle-reel-design §9.3 says config.ts refuses a full reel outside 60–80 s and a short cut outside 40–50 s. While web/reel/reel.toml lists only some vignettes (one, realtime, today: 12.2 s in full), parseReel cannot apply that check, so it lives in checkCuts, which config.test.ts exercises but no recorder or composer calls. The composition (`//web/reel:reel`, phase 2) should call it once reel.toml lists every vignette of spec §3.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":180},"end":{"line":182},"content_hash":"cfb0132daace495a1f72d9ef133ac081a4b32163497cf9da3e9d4d621e26f664"},"suggested_fix":"Call checkCuts from the composition's entry point (and the composer's own reel.toml check) when reel.toml names all nine vignettes.","summary":"Nothing calls checkCuts yet: parseReel does not hold reel.toml to the 60–80 s full and 40–50 s short cuts","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/reel.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:58:58.925763Z","id":"b1cb9ebc6897ab71a4bc79acdc82c77bd4a01a12f174a92a500dddc506edb6b6","body":{"detail":"The recorder imports only web/e2e/fixtures.ts, time.ts and hosted-helpers.ts and reads web/package.json, but //web:files is the whole web project (shell, bridge, unit tests, every e2e spec). Spec §8 lists the e2e helpers it imports as the input. A recording takes tens of seconds per vignette, and only `just reel` pays it, but a test edit invalidating every <id>_fast and later <id>_frames is wasted work. A narrower input needs web/BUILD.bazel to split the e2e helpers out of :files_tests (two copy_to_bin of one file conflict).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"c3c695679dc521554c2b9c5bfeaeb100d62971cc664d1bdbf9fe4164b434b7f0"},"suggested_fix":"In web/BUILD.bazel, a copy_to_bin of web/e2e/*.ts minus *.spec.ts (taken out of :files_tests' glob) plus package.json, and the reel's srcs name that instead of //web:files.","summary":"Every recording reads all of //web:files, so an edit to any web unit or browser test re-records every vignette","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:58:58.926Z","id":"a5b80597b38f3d77c84a282bbe5b7c03be9607b762543a58ae3ee59db7848e51","body":{"detail":"hostedDaemon in web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts calls test.skip when the daemon takes another port, which only works inside a Playwright test, so the recorder restates its [hosted] config (public_origin, setup_secret_env) and fails instead. Factoring a startHosted() that both call would keep one copy of that config, at the cost of touching the e2e helpers (and so rerunning every browser test) in the reel's first change.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":106},"end":{"line":113},"content_hash":"e84d9b83eb5558019b168d93b6a16079470631fecf0c695eeadd665dedb50911"},"summary":"Factor a test-free hosted daemon start out of web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts instead of restating its config here","tags":["revisit:the [hosted] config hostedDaemon writes changes, or a second recorder needs it","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T15:58:58.926251Z","id":"e373ab8bb26916a77a551a363ff8bf15eb0fb7a493db0131c7fb0acb29b1f7e5","body":{"detail":"Playwright's recordVideo scales a page's screencast down to fit the size it is given, never up: at size 1600 × 1000 a 1280 × 800 viewport at device scale 1.25 recorded as 1280 × 800 in the top left corner of a grey 1600 × 1000 frame. So fast mode records at the viewport's size; the capture's 1600 × 1000 device pixels (spec §5) come from deterministic mode (CDP screenshots). A reel composed from fast clips (`reel_fast`, spec §8) must scale them up or frame them smaller.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":126},"end":{"line":129},"content_hash":"f23a5ef1a46edaf27ef06dbcec997c8ae87cd341ce7c388121c513fbf4b4a81f"},"summary":"The fast clip is 1280 × 800 (the viewport's CSS size), not the capture's 1600 × 1000","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/reel.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:24.610858Z","id":"afc20ef71dc4ccd94cfb2d3a902250b55f496f77768c166ce10301d2bdd2e3c2","body":{"detail":"The recorder imports only web/e2e/fixtures.ts, time.ts and hosted-helpers.ts and reads web/package.json, but //web:files is the whole web project (shell, bridge, unit tests, every e2e spec). Spec §8 lists the e2e helpers it imports as the input. A recording takes tens of seconds per vignette, and only `just reel` pays it, but a test edit invalidating every <id>_fast and <id>_frames is wasted work. A narrower input needs web/BUILD.bazel to split the e2e helpers out of :files_tests (two copy_to_bin of one file conflict).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"c3c695679dc521554c2b9c5bfeaeb100d62971cc664d1bdbf9fe4164b434b7f0"},"suggested_fix":"In web/BUILD.bazel, a copy_to_bin of web/e2e/*.ts minus *.spec.ts (taken out of :files_tests' glob) plus package.json, and the reel's srcs name that instead of //web:files.","summary":"Every recording reads all of //web:files, so an edit to any web unit or browser test re-records every vignette","supersedes":"b1cb9ebc6897ab71a4bc79acdc82c77bd4a01a12f174a92a500dddc506edb6b6","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:25.643188Z","id":"34183bb704faa93665d8469785e43fedfdf0bfac220225c3976fce572a14680e","body":{"detail":"hostedDaemon in web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts calls test.skip when the daemon takes another port, which only works inside a Playwright test, so the recorder restates its [hosted] config (public_origin, setup_secret_env) and fails instead. Factoring a startHosted() that both call would keep one copy of that config, at the cost of touching the e2e helpers (and so rerunning every browser test) in the reel's first change.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":112},"end":{"line":122},"content_hash":"cf00ca93ad8ce8dff77717c6360b13e077db56b9664e3b5af9a71e2ca9c12f3f"},"summary":"Factor a test-free hosted daemon start out of web/e2e/hosted-helpers.ts instead of restating its config here","supersedes":"a5b80597b38f3d77c84a282bbe5b7c03be9607b762543a58ae3ee59db7848e51","tags":["revisit:the [hosted] config hostedDaemon writes changes, or a second recorder needs it","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/record.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:25.977990Z","id":"003f436301545968a3c29f12a00251583a252a98b556baea7931b694f99228e2","body":{"detail":"Playwright's recordVideo scales a page's screencast down to fit the size it is given, never up: at size 1600 × 1000 a 1280 × 800 viewport at device scale 1.25 recorded as 1280 × 800 in the top left corner of a grey 1600 × 1000 frame. So fast mode records at the viewport's size; the capture's 1600 × 1000 device pixels (spec §5) come from deterministic mode (CDP screenshots with a clip at the page's devicePixelRatio, web/reel/camera.ts). A reel composed from fast clips (`reel_fast`, spec §8) must scale them up or frame them smaller.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":135},"end":{"line":138},"content_hash":"a3cd579606f12e65f71cbf8dbb1978c9a7f0b22f2c4122db87f804fe3355af94"},"summary":"The fast clip is 1280 × 800 (the viewport's CSS size), not the capture's 1600 × 1000","supersedes":"e373ab8bb26916a77a551a363ff8bf15eb0fb7a493db0131c7fb0acb29b1f7e5","tags":["session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.131643Z","id":"51a9983becc7e62126858721009a2e0f54718a7b8c38ef8154c0830301574090","body":{"detail":"FREEZE_IN keeps each animation's first-seen time in Animation.id, the one piece of per-animation state that every JavaScript world shares (the recorder evaluates in an isolated world or over the DevTools protocol, and getAnimations() hands each world its own wrappers). A page that names its animations, reads their ids, or reads their playState or currentTime would see the recorder's values: a vignette filming such a page would show it behaving differently than it does for a person.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":49},"end":{"line":61},"content_hash":"34b11bbb1b3b1930ed0583d3cf054ab3d4f833563aa0139ae2dd952e1cb1fe24"},"suggested_fix":"Keep first-seen times recorder-side, keyed by the DevTools protocol's object identity (a RemoteObject per animation in one isolated world held for the frame's life), and leave id alone.","summary":"The deterministic camera writes `reel@<ms>` into the id of every animation on the page, and pauses them through the page's own Animation objects","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.131751Z","id":"3f211f601e38bfd9fab3b9d454aa7379837327c7772bd7bb15136fbefe7d431e","body":{"detail":"quiet() waits for the page's in-flight requests (Playwright request events: the page's frames, not its shared or service workers) and then drains each frame's task queue with a MessageChannel round trip, frames inside first and the page last, twice over. A message one renderer posts to another (the artifact frame's clax:peer-at to the shell, which places the name tags) is very likely, not certain, to have run before the screenshot. realtime.ts waits for each person's step to reach Alex's frame (clax:peers, db/changed) before the film moves on; what one renderer then tells another inside a frame is what the drain covers. //web/reel:realtime_determinism passed on its runs on one machine; a failure there names the first differing frame and keeps the pair in the test's outputs.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":212},"end":{"line":232},"content_hash":"ccc105d2800f2d28c59797512858d0f53f4753a95a44221bfad6ab65528f4ee8"},"suggested_fix":"If a pair ever differs on a tag or arrow, keep the artifact frame in the shell's process for the deterministic camera (Chromium --disable-features=IsolateOrigins,site-per-process, merged with Playwright's own --disable-features list, which a second flag would replace).","summary":"A frame is taken once the page's requests are done and each frame's queued tasks have run, which orders work inside a process but only very likely across processes","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T16:50:26.131937Z","id":"14d31b897f7d50ade6ca87cc71c7688ba4f820137ec50c733576f80403c2efde","body":{"detail":"determinism.sh runs `node reel/record.ts` twice; the recorder needs the web project laid out as bazel/js/npm_script.mjs lays it out (Node, the project's packages, the e2e helpers it imports, the warmed clax and the browsers read where Bazel put them), which a bare sh_test's runfiles do not give. The test stays tagged manual, exclusive, no-sandbox and no-remote, as a recording is.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":95},"end":{"line":99},"content_hash":"9c5f83028781f7489593f27001c3f22f5fb6c19ef1282bc1bf4727d34bd245bb"},"summary":"realtime_determinism is an npm_script_test that runs determinism.sh (pnpm run reel:determinism), not a bare sh_test","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:09.258726Z","id":"f80cdd2bd4f38fb14b796881223ace5ab712e029a0c52744f7431ded5d89f9ac","body":{"detail":"A shell document that loads anew while the camera rolls (the agent vignette's Reload, web/reel/vignettes/agent.ts) requests /_clax/shell/stream-worker-<hash>.js again (new SharedWorker in web/shell/src/stream.ts:92), and Playwright reports the request on the page (resourceType script, no sec-fetch-dest header) but never reports it finished, so quiet() waited 10 s and failed. The exemption matches that path alone; it couples the recorder to the shell's build output name.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":84},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"10818436b546fd49acf98f111ef765403dd5e55ad7c260604aa4cc1925af86af"},"suggested_fix":"Recognise a shared worker's script request by what Chromium says of it (Network.requestWillBeSent type or initiator over CDP) instead of its path.","summary":"The deterministic camera exempts the shell's shared worker script by its URL path, so a renamed or moved worker would make every Reload-type navigation stall a frame for QUIET_MS","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:09.258790Z","id":"2dcbc3afe05dc5fbec296f60ba2b454e2c102fb3846dfa17b180ce25af06e35f","body":{"detail":"Needed for a Reload during a roll: the old content frame vanished between page.frames() and its lookup, which failed the recording (no frame <v1 url>). The skipped document is reached at the next frame. A document mid-navigation that shows on a screenshot unfrozen could differ between runs; the agent vignette avoids it by waiting for the new shell in the Reload click's `landed` (web/reel/director.ts click), so no frame is taken mid-load. //web/reel:agent_determinism passes.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":230},"end":{"line":245},"content_hash":"7c5cbd9c5a38486daf58465347d839ade08957d094774c1af59a73cf2c974bf0"},"summary":"inEach skips a frame the page is replacing (detached, or not found in the frame tree by its URL): that document's animations are not frozen and its queue not drained for that one frame","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:09.258820Z","id":"e80b6b28fd36e065eb559862d2afd4cf3384791c392943526f181f1f9ce2e3d9","body":{"detail":"The daemons keep real time and have no clock a test can set (the store's clock is SystemClock, crates/clax-server/src/core.rs:145). With the camera ahead of them (2026-11-03) the agent vignette read \"7 d ago\" and a working clock of 160:30:27 that changed between two renders. Behind them, their times clamp to \"just now\" and 0:00 (web/shell/src/format.ts relativeTime, web/shell/src/view/working-model.ts clock) on any day. A ticking working clock would need a daemon clock the recorder sets.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":18},"end":{"line":25},"content_hash":"f6e9130cbc053b2e93f1da821d275d9aa2dd73b41308bf0f796b256d2bf8671c"},"summary":"REEL_EPOCH is in the past (2025-11-03): every time a daemon stamps reads \"just now\" and every working clock reads 0:00 and never ticks on film","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/reel/camera.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:59:09.258844Z","id":"9d6e385e43cefe45bf1dda81a51a2ccb019811fdf23eb31fb1e5a6d89c0b9ecb","body":{"detail":"The caret blinks on the browser's own timer, which page.clock does not hold: //web/reel:agent_determinism failed on frames 173-184 where one run showed the composer's caret and the other did not. Playwright's own screenshots hide the caret by default for the same reason.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":68},"end":{"line":78},"content_hash":"d0248b0e8ff67da306d76159bcfda68d3e541bed581d558183ddafadf37b341e"},"summary":"The deterministic camera hides every text caret (NO_CARET), so the film shows no caret while Alex types","tags":["reel","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
